<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description> (255-char cap), and it is INSIDE
        the root element on purpose - a comment ABOVE <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy.

        THE CANONICAL RATIONALE IS ON THE LEAD TWIN,
        objects/Lead/fields/Extraction_Score_Pct__c. That file enumerates the nine
        signed-off deal-process keys, records why the six physical-property keys are
        excluded, and states the fail-soft contract. It is recorded ONCE, there, so the two
        cannot drift into two different denominators.

        THE SCORE IS A SNAPSHOT OF THE INTAKE, AND IT IS NEVER RECOMPUTED HERE. It records
        how complete the ORIGINAL broker email was. An analyst who later types the missing
        guidance price by hand does NOT move this number, and that is correct: it measures
        the automation, not the record. Reading it as "how complete is this deal record?"
        will be wrong the moment anyone edits the Opportunity. Do not add a recompute.

        NOT Parse_Confidence__c, which is also carried to Opportunity and answers a
        different question (the model's certainty about is_acquisition_related). A HIGH
        confidence does not imply a high score and a low score does not impeach the
        classification. Both are retained side by side; conflating them is a defect.

        NULL is meaningful: it reads "not scored" - the fail-soft path - which is not zero.
    -->
    <fullName>Extraction_Score_Pct__c</fullName>
    <description>Percent of the nine signed-off deal-process extraction keys captured from the original broker email, carried from the Lead at conversion. A snapshot of the intake; never recomputed. Null means not scored, which is not zero.</description>
    <externalId>false</externalId>
    <inlineHelpText>How complete the automated extraction of the original broker email was, 0-100. It does not change when someone edits this deal by hand.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Extraction Score %</label>
    <precision>3</precision>
    <required>false</required>
    <scale>0</scale>
    <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Number</type>
    <unique>false</unique>
</CustomField>
